@@ -0,0 +1,80 @@
+# Daily Grind security audit and deployment
+
+The site is a static coffee shop page served by a small Node HTTP server. Its
+resource inventory supports an enforced Content Security Policy without allowing
+scripts or inline styles. Security headers are applied by `request-handler.js`
+using `security.js`; deployments must route traffic through that handler or
+replicate these headers at the hosting layer.
+
+## Audit findings and changes
+
+| Surface | Finding | Implemented measure |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| HTML and CSS | A style block and heading style attribute required inline CSS. | Moved styling to `/styles.css` and a class; `style-src 'self'` and `style-src-attr 'none'` block injected styles. |
+| Client scripts | No scripts, event handlers, DOM sinks, messaging, storage, workers, or third-party script dependencies exist. | `script-src 'none'` blocks all scripts; Trusted Types sink enforcement and `trusted-types 'none'` block policy creation in supporting browsers. No bypass policy or extra runtime script was added. |
+| External resources | One background image uses `https://images.unsplash.com`; fonts are system fonts. | Allowlisted that exact image origin; all other resource classes default to blocked. Existing image retained. |
+| Injection and framing | No security headers were present. | CSP blocks plugins, base tags, frames and outbound script connections; forms target the same origin; `frame-ancestors 'self'` and `X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN` protect framing. |
+| Browser capabilities | No camera, microphone, geolocation, payment, USB, or cross-origin popup integrations exist. | Disabled unused permissions; added conservative opener and resource policies, MIME sniffing protection and referrer restrictions. |
+| Request isolation | Cross-site resource requests were unrestricted. | Fetch Metadata rejects foreign subresources and state-changing requests, including from sibling subdomains; public top-level GET/HEAD navigation remains allowed. `Vary` includes the evaluated metadata headers. |
+| Logout | A GET link returned a message without clearing browser data. | Uses a POST form, checks Fetch Metadata and exact Origin, disables caching, and returns `Clear-Site-Data` for cookies, storage and cache. |
+| Reporting | No violation telemetry existed. | Modern Reporting API and legacy CSP reporting target `/security-reports`. Bodies are limited to 16 KiB, batches to 100 CSP reports, and logs contain only fixed directive/disposition counts. |
+
+The server still returns the page for existing document routes. Only a fixed
+stylesheet path serves CSS; arbitrary paths cannot expose server or policy files.
+GET/HEAD, logout POST, and reporting POST are handled explicitly with correct MIME
+types. Security headers also accompany error responses.
+
+## Policy rollout
+
+The default is **enforced CSP**, based on the complete static resource inventory.
+For a deployment with additional CDN injections or integrations, set
+`CSP_REPORT_ONLY=1` in its process environment to observe the candidate CSP first.
+Companion headers, request filtering, and logout checks remain enforced in this
+mode. Collect representative traffic, triage extension noise and repeatable
+first-party violations, then remove this setting to enforce the candidate. Keep
+reporting enabled after promotion. Do not broadly allow scripts or inline styles
+to silence unexplained reports.
+
+`Reporting-Endpoints` uses a same-origin relative endpoint, with `report-to csp`
+and `report-uri /security-reports` for older implementations. Reporting delivery
+is browser dependent and requires a trustworthy deployment context; receiving no
+reports is not proof that every policy is compatible. The reporting endpoint is
+unauthenticated because browser reports are untrusted telemetry. Apply request
+rate limits at the production edge and disable raw request-body logging there.
+The application never logs report URLs, query strings, samples, cookies or user
+agents. Script samples are deliberately not requested.
+
+Serve production traffic over HTTPS at the deployment edge. After TLS is working,
+set `HTTPS_DEPLOYMENT=1` to enable a short HSTS policy (`max-age=300`) and HTTPS
+Origin checks for logout. The proxy must preserve the public Host header.
+Arbitrary forwarded protocol headers are ignored. Raise the HSTS duration only
+after confirming HTTPS coverage; subdomain coverage and preload are not enabled.
+Preserve response security headers and route the report endpoint through the proxy.
+
+Cross-origin embedder isolation is omitted because the site does not need shared
+memory and its external image has not been audited for that restriction. No
+wildcard CORS grants are added. Trusted Types support varies; the no-script CSP
+remains the primary injection defense. Future scripts must undergo a policy
+review and use narrowly authorized hashes or per-response nonces.
+
+Logout currently has no server session to invalidate. If authentication is added,
+invalidate the server session and expire its cookie as well; browser data clearing
+requires a secure context and does not replace session revocation. Use HttpOnly,
+Secure, SameSite cookies and retain the POST origin protections.
+
+## Offline validation
+
+Run `npm test`, `npm run build`, and `git diff --check`. The tests use in-memory
+request/response doubles, import only modules without a listening socket, and
+check header configuration, markup compatibility, resource MIME types, request
+isolation, logout protections, report validation and log privacy. The build only
+checks JavaScript syntax. These checks do not verify deployed proxy headers or
+real browser reporting delivery. No server startup or browser interaction is
+required.
+
+## Platform references
+
+- [MDN Content Security Policy](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Guides/CSP)
+- [MDN Trusted Types directive](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Reference/Headers/Content-Security-Policy/trusted-types)
+- [MDN CSP reporting directive](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Reference/Headers/Content-Security-Policy/report-to)
+- [W3C Reporting API endpoint processing](https://w3c.github.io/reporting/#process-header)
